@* Dropdown (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/overlay.css</code></li>
    <li>Tag helpers <code>&lt;dnf-dropdown&gt;</code> and its items in <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Components/DropdownTagHelpers.cs</code></li>
    <li>Behaviour <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/wwwroot/dnf.js</code> (placement, keyboard)</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A button that opens a menu of actions: row and card actions, the account menu, the theme menu. The menu is a native
    popover, so it opens in the browser's top layer - no table scroll area, card or stacking order clips or covers it - and
    the browser closes it on Escape and on a click outside. Use <code>&lt;dnf-dropdown&gt;</code> with its item tag helpers.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="text-trigger">
    <dnf-dropdown label="Options" text="Options" variant="Secondary" size="Md" placement="bottom-start">
        <dnf-dropdown-label>Theme</dnf-dropdown-label>
        <dnf-dropdown-button role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="true">System</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-button role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false">Light</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-separator />
        <dnf-dropdown-link href="#text-trigger" icon="external-link" new-tab="true">Open site</dnf-dropdown-link>
    </dnf-dropdown>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

