<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown</code></td><td>block</td><td>the wrapper (<code>inline-block</code>, relative)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__menu</code></td><td>element</td><td>the popover panel: fixed, at least 12rem wide, scrolls when taller than the window, raised surface, <code>--dnf-radius-lg</code>, medium shadow; forms inside have no margin</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__item</code></td><td>element</td><td>a full-width row (link or button) with icon and text</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__item--danger</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>danger text</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__label</code></td><td>element</td><td>a small subtle heading over a group</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__separator</code></td><td>element</td><td>a 1px line</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__chevron</code></td><td>element</td><td>a text trigger's <code>chevron-down</code> icon; turns up while its button is <code>aria-expanded="true"</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-dropdown__note</code></td><td>element</td><td>a short wrapped explanation in <code>text-xs</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>hover / keyboard focus</td><td><code>.dnf-dropdown__item:is(:hover, :focus-visible)</code></td><td>surface-hover background</td></tr>
        <tr><td>disabled</td><td><code>:disabled</code>, <code>[aria-disabled="true"]</code></td><td>55% opacity, no pointer events</td></tr>
        <tr><td>checked</td><td><code>[aria-checked="true"]</code></td><td>a check mark at the end (radio and checkbox items)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>open</td><td><code>:popover-open</code>; <code>dnf.js</code> adds <code>data-open</code> to the menu and <code>aria-expanded="true"</code> to the button</td><td>fades and scales in, fades out on close; instant without browser support or with reduced motion</td></tr>
        <tr><td>trigger open</td><td><code>[aria-expanded="true"] &gt; .dnf-dropdown__chevron</code></td><td>the chevron turns up (animated)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<h3 id="api-dropdown"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownTagHelper)" />
<p>Renders the wrapper, the button (<code>popovertarget</code>, <code>aria-haspopup="menu"</code>, <code>aria-expanded="false"</code>;
    with <code>text</code> a label and a chevron, else the icon and <code>aria-label</code>) and the menu (<code>popover</code>,
    <code>role="menu"</code>, <code>aria-label</code>, <code>data-placement</code>) with a generated id. <code>Xl</code> renders the
    large size. <code>class</code> is appended to the wrapper.</p>

<h3 id="api-dropdown-link"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown-link&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownLinkTagHelper)" />
<p>An <code>&lt;a class="dnf-dropdown__item" role="menuitem"&gt;</code>; <code>href</code> and other attributes pass through,
    <code>class</code> is appended.</p>

<h3 id="api-dropdown-button"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown-button&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownButtonTagHelper)" />
<p>A <code>&lt;button type="button" class="dnf-dropdown__item" role="menuitem"&gt;</code> for client-side actions. <code>role</code>
    (<code>menuitemradio</code>, <code>menuitemcheckbox</code> with <code>aria-checked</code>), <code>type</code>, <code>disabled</code>
    and <code>data-*</code> pass through; <code>class</code> is appended.</p>

<h3 id="api-dropdown-post"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown-post&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownPostTagHelper)" />
<p><code>field-name="value"</code> adds <code>&lt;input type="hidden" name="name" value="value"&gt;</code> (one per attribute). The
    child content is the item's text.</p>

<h3 id="api-dropdown-label"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown-label&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownLabelTagHelper)" />
<p>A <code>&lt;div class="dnf-dropdown__label" role="presentation"&gt;</code>.</p>

<h3 id="api-dropdown-separator"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown-separator&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownSeparatorTagHelper)" />
<p>A <code>&lt;div class="dnf-dropdown__separator" role="separator"&gt;</code>; self-closing.</p>

<h3 id="api-dropdown-note"><code>&lt;dnf-dropdown-note&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfDropdownNoteTagHelper)" />
<p>A <code>&lt;span class="dnf-dropdown__note"&gt;</code>. On the label, separator and note, too, <code>class</code> is appended.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The button has <code>aria-haspopup="menu"</code> and <code>aria-expanded</code>; an icon-only one is named by <code>label</code>.</li>
    <li>Opened from the keyboard, focus moves to the first item; ArrowDown and ArrowUp (wrapping), Home and End move between
        items; Escape closes the menu (the browser) and focus returns to the button. A click on an item closes it.</li>
    <li>Items are <code>role="menuitem"</code>, or <code>menuitemradio</code> / <code>menuitemcheckbox</code> with
        <code>aria-checked</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use the tag helpers for row and card menus - never hand-build a POST item without the antiforgery token.</li>
    <li>Do keep destructive items last, after a separator, with <code>danger="true"</code> and <code>confirm</code>.</li>
    <li>Don't put form fields in a menu - use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/popover">popover</a> or a
        <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/dialog">dialog</a>.</li>
</ul>
